@@ -130,6 +130,24 @@ The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each hold
 
 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-spec-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse of the veterinarian directory: a specialty directory. It lists every specialty by its stored name, and under each specialty the veterinarians who hold it. Each veterinarian is shown by full name, first name before last name — "Helen Leary", not "Leary, Helen". A veterinarian holding no specialty is not dropped. They appear under a grouping for having none, so the page accounts for every specialty and for the veterinarians who hold none, without becoming the full veterinarian roster. The directory is one page — every specialty renders together, with no pagination `[REQ-SPEC-001]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it shown by full name in first-name-then-last-name order.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a specialty held by more than one veterinarian, when the directory is opened, then every veterinarian holding that specialty appears under it.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given a veterinarian who holds no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears under the grouping for holding none.
+- `[REQ-SPEC-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the directory is opened, then all of them render on a single page with no pagination controls.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. Specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one, and the veterinarians under each specialty are likewise in a stable order.
+2. The grouping for veterinarians holding no specialty appears only when at least one veterinarian holds none.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
 ### Language
 
 <a id="req-lang-001"></a><a id="req-lang-002"></a>
